-- ============================================================================
-- DR5 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Geomechanics and Wellbore Stability, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, so the seeded structure and the
-- shipped lesson files cannot disagree.
--
-- What this tier owns: the 1D mechanical earth model. Six numbers at a depth,
-- of which TWO are never measured on a normal well. The overburden as an
-- integral of a density log that nobody runs over the top of a hole. The pore
-- pressure taken from upstream, deliberately, so a geomechanics answer can
-- never smuggle in a circular pore pressure argument. The two horizontal
-- stresses from one formula differing only in the order of two tectonic
-- strains, so their entire difference is tectonic and comes to 3906250 Pa at
-- every depth in this profile. k0 as nu over one minus nu. Strength from two
-- published sonic correlations. And the frictional bounds, which are a BOUND
-- rather than an estimate, with the clamps counted and reported.
--
-- THE FINDING THE FIXTURE'S OWN OUTPUT PRODUCES, AND m05 IS BUILT ON. Twenty
-- three of the profile's 52 samples put SHmax ABOVE the overburden, which is
-- not the normal faulting regime the run assumes. They are the 23 shallowest,
-- contiguous from 50 m to 1150 m, and all on the same condition. Only FOUR of
-- them are clamped, so 19 got there through the estimate alone: the tectonic
-- strain term is fixed at 8897569.444444442 Pa for SHmax while the burial term
-- grows with depth, so at 50 m the strain term is twelve times the burial part
-- and at 2600 m about a fifth of it. The quality score reports 80 for exactly
-- that. A depth-independent addition to a depth-proportional quantity is only
-- safe where the two are comparable, and the model has no mechanism to notice.
--
-- A SECOND FINDING, IN m04. Horsrud and McNally cross TWICE, at about
-- 198.68499251376295 and about 409.8356528477385 microseconds per metre, and
-- both crossings fall inside this profile's sonic range of 188 to 494. So
-- there is no rule about which of the two is the conservative choice, and at
-- the deepest readings the SHALE correlation gives the larger strength, which
-- in a stability calculation is the less conservative direction.
--
-- Every number in the lessons is derived by running the vendored
-- engines/drilling geomech module against its own goldens, and the teaching
-- lab the panels and this course share is pinned by geomechLab.test.js. A
-- numeric sweep over the lessons resolved all 315 literals carrying seven or
-- more significant figures to an engine-derived value; a tier-leakage sweep
-- over the lessons and the banks reports zero downward leaks and zero
-- same-tier answer prints against all eighteen graded fields.
--
-- Answer keys live only here and in academy_quiz_questions, which has no
-- client SELECT policy.
-- ============================================================================

